    <title>Calibrated Early Stopping under
  Distribution Shift</title>
    <updated>2024-06-10T17:59:59Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.01234v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.01234v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We propose a calibrated early stopping rule for models trained under covariate
shift. Across nine shifted benchmarks the rule reduces expected calibration error
by 23% relative to validation-loss stopping. It does not change top-1 accuracy.
</summary>
